**Convention 11.2 (cases retained by the construction).** Relative empty suffixes and multiple indices at one node are literal trie markers. Entirely unobserved children are $\#$, with exact four-type capacities. Early alpha and beta leaves include all their absent descendants. Closed pieces such as $E$ and singleton image response cells retain their exact counts; there is no assumption that an observed cell is infinite. Whole-class distinctness is enforced across all six values, and partner repetition is enforced at both occurrences. Duplicate and unused preparer or serving states count and remain in the full indexed relation. An initial Halt and a Halt reached after the last permitted call need no further native call. Cycles are permitted in installed graphs and only the actual selected bounded paths must terminate. The case $m=0$ has only constant branch observations and cannot produce both bits, although Theorem 8.3 still gives relation-preserving normalization.

